1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:05,100
Good afternoon, my name is Juliet Heckman, and I'm a junior at Leon High School here in Tallahassee, Florida.

2
00:00:06,960 --> 00:00:13,220
Over the past two and a half years, I've had the privilege of taking four AP courses, three of which have been history-related.

3
00:00:14,180 --> 00:00:22,560
These classes have further advanced my knowledge of the world around me, as each class offers thorough evidence, viewpoints, and reasoning based on its designated topic.

4
00:00:22,560 --> 00:00:30,880
When I heard the news that there was an AP course in the works that was designated specifically to African American studies, I was grateful.

5
00:00:31,580 --> 00:00:39,620
Grateful in the sense that this side of history, one which is notoriously ignored and disregarded, would finally be given the proper and sufficient representation that it deserves.

6
00:00:41,100 --> 00:00:47,020
I was grateful that there was an interdisciplinary course that not only goes into depth on the history of African Americans,

7
00:00:47,020 --> 00:00:52,940
but also emphasizes the contributions made by them that have built the foundation of our country itself.

8
00:00:55,180 --> 00:01:00,660
Now, you can only imagine how me and many of my classmates felt when we recently learned that, because we live in the state of Florida,

9
00:01:00,880 --> 00:01:06,440
we would not be given the opportunity to take this course, because it, and I quote, lacks educational value.

10
00:01:08,040 --> 00:01:13,480
Every single AP course that I have taken has significantly advanced my knowledge and understanding of our world,

11
00:01:13,480 --> 00:01:17,640
and has inspired me to learn more, and I have full confidence that this course would be no different.

12
00:01:18,620 --> 00:01:25,060
Simply because Florida lawmakers may be uncomfortable or even afraid with the course's criteria, because it is too woke,

13
00:01:25,300 --> 00:01:29,300
does not grant them the right to take away this opportunity from thousands of students across the state.

14
00:01:31,060 --> 00:01:35,940
Times are changing, education is expanding, and students have higher levels of curiosity than ever before.

15
00:01:35,940 --> 00:01:41,860
It is not fair for our education to be constricted under the ignorant opinions of those who reject a course

16
00:01:41,860 --> 00:01:49,710
that is designed to only advance our understanding of the world around us.

17
00:01:50,150 --> 00:01:51,910
This is not a course of indoctrination.

18
00:01:52,430 --> 00:01:57,210
It's a course that dives deep into the history, culture, arts, literature, and advancements

19
00:01:57,210 --> 00:02:00,030
that African Americans have and continue to make in our country.

20
00:02:00,390 --> 00:02:05,990
A greater understanding of this honest history is necessary in order to fully comprehend our country's origins

21
00:02:05,990 --> 00:02:09,010
and the contributions that have been made to lead us to where we are today.

22
00:02:12,550 --> 00:02:14,010
Let me tell you something about Black folks.

23
00:02:15,510 --> 00:02:17,430
We're going to cheer you on when you're saying a word.

24
00:02:17,790 --> 00:02:18,490
They was in the back.

